@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `law08-vintage`
IMPORT `law08-nouns`
IMPORT `law08-ch7-commencement`

-- Chuong III, Muc 7-9 (Dieu 109-123): financial safety, solvency, the three supervisory measures
-- (improvement, early intervention, control), dissolution, bankruptcy, disclosure of information, loss
-- prevention and anti-fraud. Dieu 109-114 and 116 do not take effect until 1 January 2028 in V1 and
-- 1 January 2031 from V2 (Dieu 156(2)); a rule on them takes the day of the question and declines before it.
-- Dieu 117(3) is repealed by Law 139/2025/QH15 Dieu 2(7) from V2. Working days (Dieu 117) are an input
-- calendar (fork F23).

§ `Chuong III, Muc 7: Kha nang thanh toan va bien phap can thiep`

§§ `Dieu 109: financial safety`

@@q 2290 2297
@ref Dieu 109 (src:2290-2297)
GIVEN p IS A `A financial safety position`
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 109(1): the insurer is financially safe on the day` p `the day in question` MEANS
    IF `Dieu 156(2): the provision is in force on the day` `Dieu 109` `the day in question`
    THEN p's `meets the rules on capital` AND p's `meets the rules on solvency` AND p's `meets the rules on investment`
    ELSE REFUSE "Dieu 109 is not yet in force on that day (Dieu 156(2)); the old Law's provision, not among the sources, governs until then"

@@q 2298 2300
@ref Dieu 109 (src:2298-2300)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 109(3): the cases in which the Minister of Finance applies improvement, early intervention or control measures` MEANS
    REFUSE "Dieu 109(3) leaves to the Minister of Finance the cases in which Dieu 111, 112 and 113 apply; the Minister's circular is not among the sources"

§§ `Dieu 110: solvency`

@@q 2302 2308
@ref Dieu 110 (src:2302-2308)
GIVEN p IS A `A financial safety position`
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 110(2): the insurer has sufficient solvency on the day` p `the day in question` MEANS
    IF `Dieu 156(2): the provision is in force on the day` `Dieu 110` `the day in question`
    THEN p's `has set aside technical reserves in full` AND p's `has assured the capital adequacy ratio`
    ELSE REFUSE "Dieu 110 is not yet in force on that day (Dieu 156(2)); the old Law's provision, not among the sources, governs until then"

§§ `Dieu 111: improvement measures`

-- Dieu 111(3). While carrying out improvement measures the insurer may not transfer profit abroad, distribute
-- profit or pay dividends, or take on more reinsurance.
@@q 2330 2334
@ref Dieu 111 (src:2330-2334)
GIVEN a IS AN `An activity during a supervisory measure`
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 111(3): the activity is prohibited during improvement measures` a `the day in question` MEANS
    IF `Dieu 156(2): the provision is in force on the day` `Dieu 111` `the day in question`
    THEN a's `transfers profit abroad, distributes profit or pays dividends` OR a's `takes on more reinsurance`
    ELSE REFUSE "Dieu 111 is not yet in force on that day (Dieu 156(2))"

§§ `Dieu 112: early intervention`

-- Dieu 112(1). The Ministry of Finance issues the order when the ratio is at the early-intervention level (the
-- level is the Minister's, Dieu 109(3): an input flag) or improvement measures applied for 12 continuous months
-- have not restored it.
@@q 2336 2342
@ref Dieu 112 (src:2336-2342)
GIVEN m IS A `A supervisory measure`
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 112(1): the Ministry of Finance issues an early intervention order` m `the day in question` MEANS
    IF `Dieu 156(2): the provision is in force on the day` `Dieu 112` `the day in question`
    THEN m's `the capital adequacy ratio is at the level that requires early intervention` OR m's `improvement measures were applied for 12 continuous months without restoring the ratio`
    ELSE REFUSE "Dieu 112 is not yet in force on that day (Dieu 156(2))"

-- Dieu 112(2)-(3), (6): 60 days to build the remedial plan, at most 12 months to carry it out; if the plan is not
-- built in 60 days, or the ratio is not restored in 12 months, the Ministry requires one or more of the Dieu 112(4) measures.
@@q 2343 2352
@ref Dieu 112 (src:2343-2352)
GIVEN m IS A `A supervisory measure`
GIVETH A DATE
`Dieu 112(2): the last day to build and report the remedial plan` m MEANS
    m's `date of the Ministry of Finance's order` PLUS 60

GIVEN m IS A `A supervisory measure`
GIVETH A DATE
`Dieu 112(3): the last day to carry out the remedial plan` m MEANS
    `add months` (m's `date of the Ministry of Finance's order`) 12

@@q 2364 2372
@ref Dieu 112 (src:2364-2372)
GIVEN m IS A `A supervisory measure`
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 112(6): the Ministry of Finance may require the Dieu 112(4) measures on the day` m `the day in question` MEANS
        (    `the day in question` ABOVE `Dieu 112(2): the last day to build and report the remedial plan` m
         AND (   CONSIDER m's `date the insurer built and reported its remedial plan`
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
                 WHEN JUST x THEN x ABOVE `Dieu 112(2): the last day to build and report the remedial plan` m))
    OR  (    `the day in question` ABOVE `Dieu 112(3): the last day to carry out the remedial plan` m
         AND (   CONSIDER m's `date the ratio was restored`
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
                 WHEN JUST x THEN x ABOVE `Dieu 112(3): the last day to carry out the remedial plan` m))

-- Dieu 112(5). The activities barred during early intervention: those of Dieu 111(3), buying back own shares,
-- widening content, scope or term of activity.
@@q 2358 2363
@ref Dieu 112 (src:2358-2363)
GIVEN a IS AN `An activity during a supervisory measure`
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 112(5): the activity is prohibited during early intervention` a `the day in question` MEANS
    IF `Dieu 156(2): the provision is in force on the day` `Dieu 112` `the day in question`
    THEN     a's `transfers profit abroad, distributes profit or pays dividends`
          OR a's `takes on more reinsurance`
          OR a's `buys back its own shares`
          OR a's `widens the content, scope or term of activity`
    ELSE REFUSE "Dieu 112 is not yet in force on that day (Dieu 156(2))"

-- Dieu 112(8). The Ministry may end early intervention once an independent auditor confirms the ratio is restored,
-- or once control measures are applied.
@@q 2376 2380
@ref Dieu 112 (src:2376-2380)
GIVEN m IS A `A supervisory measure`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 112(8): the Ministry of Finance may end the early intervention` m MEANS
        (    isJust (m's `date the ratio was restored`)
         AND m's `the restoration was confirmed by an independent auditor`)
    OR  m's `a control measure has been applied`

§§ `Dieu 113: control measures`

-- Dieu 113(1). The Ministry considers and decides to order control when the ratio is at the control level (an input flag).
@@q 2382 2386
@ref Dieu 113 (src:2382-2386)
GIVEN m IS A `A supervisory measure`
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 113(1): the Ministry of Finance may order control measures` m `the day in question` MEANS
    IF `Dieu 156(2): the provision is in force on the day` `Dieu 113` `the day in question`
    THEN m's `the capital adequacy ratio is at the level that requires control`
    ELSE REFUSE "Dieu 113 is not yet in force on that day (Dieu 156(2))"

-- Dieu 113(3)-(5): 30 days to hire an independent auditor (else the Ministry appoints one); 120 days to build and
-- begin the remedial plan; at most 18 months to carry it out.
@@q 2396 2416
@ref Dieu 113 (src:2396-2416)
GIVEN m IS A `A supervisory measure`
GIVETH A DATE
`Dieu 113(3): the last day to hire an independent auditor` m MEANS
    m's `date of the Ministry of Finance's order` PLUS 30

GIVEN m IS A `A supervisory measure`
GIVETH A DATE
`Dieu 113(4): the last day to build and report the remedial plan` m MEANS
    m's `date of the Ministry of Finance's order` PLUS 120

GIVEN m IS A `A supervisory measure`
GIVETH A DATE
`Dieu 113(5): the last day to carry out the remedial plan` m MEANS
    `add months` (m's `date of the Ministry of Finance's order`) 18

GIVEN m IS A `A supervisory measure`
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 113(3): the Ministry of Finance appoints the independent auditor on the day` m `the day in question` MEANS
    `the day in question` ABOVE `Dieu 113(3): the last day to hire an independent auditor` m
    AND (   CONSIDER m's `date the insurer hired an independent auditor`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST x THEN x ABOVE `Dieu 113(3): the last day to hire an independent auditor` m)

-- Dieu 113(8): if the plan is not built in 120 days or the ratio is not restored in 18 months, the Ministry takes
-- one or more of four measures.
@@q 2429 2444
@ref Dieu 113 (src:2429-2444)
GIVEN m IS A `A supervisory measure`
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 113(8): the Ministry of Finance may take the Dieu 113(8) measures on the day` m `the day in question` MEANS
        (    `the day in question` ABOVE `Dieu 113(4): the last day to build and report the remedial plan` m
         AND (   CONSIDER m's `date the insurer built and reported its remedial plan`
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
                 WHEN JUST x THEN x ABOVE `Dieu 113(4): the last day to build and report the remedial plan` m))
    OR  (    `the day in question` ABOVE `Dieu 113(5): the last day to carry out the remedial plan` m
         AND (   CONSIDER m's `date the ratio was restored`
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
                 WHEN JUST x THEN x ABOVE `Dieu 113(5): the last day to carry out the remedial plan` m))

-- Dieu 113(7): the barred activities: those of Dieu 112(5), founding or funding an enterprise or buying real estate
-- (other than premises and storage for operations), high-risk assets or business that lowers the ratio.
@@q 2420 2428
@ref Dieu 113 (src:2420-2428)
GIVEN a IS AN `An activity during a supervisory measure`
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 113(7): the activity is prohibited during control` a `the day in question` MEANS
    IF `Dieu 156(2): the provision is in force on the day` `Dieu 113` `the day in question`
    THEN     a's `transfers profit abroad, distributes profit or pays dividends`
          OR a's `takes on more reinsurance`
          OR a's `buys back its own shares`
          OR a's `widens the content, scope or term of activity`
          OR a's `contributes capital to found an enterprise, or buys real estate other than for its own premises or storage serving its operations`
          OR a's `invests in high-risk assets or does business that lowers the ratio`
    ELSE REFUSE "Dieu 113 is not yet in force on that day (Dieu 156(2))"

@@q 2469 2482
@ref Dieu 114 (src:2469-2482)
`Dieu 114 — extra responsibilities of an insurer under improvement, early intervention or control: manage and keep assets safe; answer for the accuracy of information; report results monthly or on request; other duties (a list of duties; in force on the day Dieu 156(2) fixes)` MEANS
    "Four duties, one of them a monthly report."

§§ `Dieu 115: dissolution`

@@q 2485 2498
@ref Dieu 115 (src:2485-2498)
GIVEN d IS A `A dissolution`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 115(1): a ground for dissolving the insurer or ending the foreign branch exists` d MEANS
        d's `the enterprise asked voluntarily`
    OR  d's `the term of operation in the licence has ended`
    OR  d's `the licence was revoked under Dieu 75(1)(a), (b), (d) or (e)`
    OR  d's `a foreign branch did not restore the ratio after the period of control`
    OR  d's `another case the law provides`

GIVEN d IS A `A dissolution`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 115(2): the dissolution or ending may go ahead` d MEANS
    `Dieu 115(1): a ground for dissolving the insurer or ending the foreign branch exists` d AND d's `the Ministry of Finance approved in writing`

@@q 2499 2501
@ref Dieu 115 (src:2499-2501)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 115(3): the Government's rules on dissolving an insurer and ending a foreign branch` MEANS
    REFUSE "Dieu 115(3) delegates the conditions, dossier and procedure to the Government; its decree is not among the sources"

§§ `Dieu 116: bankruptcy`

-- Dieu 116(3)-(4). The assets go in five ranks: bankruptcy costs; employees' wages and benefits; accepted claims,
-- surrender values and refunds; State debts and creditors; owners. A rank is paid in full before the next; if the
-- assets do not cover a rank, its creditors are paid in proportion to their claims.
@@q 2515 2533
@ref Dieu 116 (src:2515-2533)
GIVEN b IS A `A bankruptcy distribution`
      r IS A `A rank in bankruptcy`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the claims of the rank` b r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `costs of bankruptcy` THEN b's `bankruptcy costs`
    WHEN `employees` THEN b's `wages, severance, social and health insurance owed to employees`
    WHEN `accepted insurance claims, surrender values and premium refunds` THEN b's `claims for compensation or payment already accepted, surrender values, account values or premium refunds`
    WHEN `State, unsecured creditors and under-secured creditors` THEN b's `obligations to the State, unsecured debts on the list, and secured debts not covered by the security`
    WHEN `owners, members and shareholders` THEN b's `claims of the owners, members and shareholders`

GIVEN b IS A `A bankruptcy distribution`
      r IS A `A rank in bankruptcy`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the assets left for the rank` b r MEANS
    max 0 (b's `assets to be divided` MINUS `the claims ahead of the rank` b r)

GIVEN b IS A `A bankruptcy distribution`
      r IS A `A rank in bankruptcy`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the claims ahead of the rank` b r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `costs of bankruptcy` THEN 0
    WHEN `employees` THEN `the claims of the rank` b `costs of bankruptcy`
    WHEN `accepted insurance claims, surrender values and premium refunds` THEN `the claims of the rank` b `costs of bankruptcy` PLUS `the claims of the rank` b `employees`
    WHEN `State, unsecured creditors and under-secured creditors` THEN `the claims of the rank` b `costs of bankruptcy` PLUS `the claims of the rank` b `employees` PLUS `the claims of the rank` b `accepted insurance claims, surrender values and premium refunds`
    WHEN `owners, members and shareholders` THEN `the claims of the rank` b `costs of bankruptcy` PLUS `the claims of the rank` b `employees` PLUS `the claims of the rank` b `accepted insurance claims, surrender values and premium refunds` PLUS `the claims of the rank` b `State, unsecured creditors and under-secured creditors`

GIVEN b IS A `A bankruptcy distribution`
      r IS A `A rank in bankruptcy`
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Dieu 116(3)-(4): the share of each claim of the rank that is paid` b r `the day in question` MEANS
    IF NOT `Dieu 156(2): the provision is in force on the day` `Dieu 116` `the day in question`
    THEN REFUSE "Dieu 116 is not yet in force on that day (Dieu 156(2)); the old Law's provision, not among the sources, governs until then"
    ELSE IF `the claims of the rank` b r AT MOST 0
         THEN REFUSE "Dieu 116: there are no claims at this rank"
         ELSE min 1 (`the assets left for the rank` b r DIVIDED BY `the claims of the rank` b r)

@@q 2503 2514
@ref Dieu 116 (src:2503-2514)
`Dieu 116(1)-(2), (5) — after the Ministry ends control under Dieu 113(11)(c) the insurer must apply to the court for bankruptcy, failing which the Ministry applies; the court goes straight to liquidation with no creditors' meeting or rehabilitation; matters not covered follow the Bankruptcy Law (procedure before the court; not evaluated here)` MEANS
    "Court procedure, outside the sources."

§ `Chuong III, Muc 8: Cong khai thong tin`

§§ `Dieu 117: duty to disclose`

-- A working day: a day that is not a Saturday or Sunday and not in the calendar of non-working days supplied as an
-- input. The Law says "ngay lam viec" here, and "ngay" elsewhere (fork F1, F23).
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the non-working days supplied` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the next working day after` d `the non-working days supplied` MEANS
    IF `is weekend` (d PLUS 1) OR elem (d PLUS 1) `the non-working days supplied`
    THEN `the next working day after` (d PLUS 1) `the non-working days supplied`
    ELSE d PLUS 1

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      n IS A NUMBER
      `the non-working days supplied` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day n working days after` d n `the non-working days supplied` MEANS
    IF n AT MOST 0
    THEN d
    ELSE `the day n working days after` (`the next working day after` d `the non-working days supplied`) (n MINUS 1) `the non-working days supplied`

-- Dieu 117(2): publish on the insurer's website within 7 working days of the end of the period for sending a periodic
-- report (Dieu 118) or of an event of regular information (Dieu 119), or within 3 working days of an event of unusual
-- information (Dieu 120).
@@q 2559 2563
@ref Dieu 117 (src:2559-2563)
GIVEN e IS A `A disclosure event`
      `the non-working days supplied` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`Dieu 117(2): the last day to publish the information` e `the non-working days supplied` MEANS
    CONSIDER e's `kind`
    WHEN `periodic information (Dieu 118)` THEN `the day n working days after` (e's `date the period for sending the report ended, or the event occurred`) 7 `the non-working days supplied`
    WHEN `regular information (Dieu 119)`  THEN `the day n working days after` (e's `date the period for sending the report ended, or the event occurred`) 7 `the non-working days supplied`
    WHEN `unusual information (Dieu 120)`  THEN `the day n working days after` (e's `date the period for sending the report ended, or the event occurred`) 3 `the non-working days supplied`

-- Dieu 117(3), V1 only: notify the Ministry of the content published within 7 working days of publishing.
-- Law 139/2025/QH15 Dieu 2(7) repeals it from V2: V2 and V3 answer that it does not exist.
@@q 2564 2566
@@qa 336 337
@ref Dieu 117 (src:2564-2566; src:law139-2025-qh15:336-337)
GIVEN e IS A `A disclosure event`
      `the non-working days supplied` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`Dieu 117(3): the last day to notify the Ministry of Finance of what was published` e `the non-working days supplied` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the rules in force are those of V2 or later`
           THEN REFUSE "Dieu 117(3) is repealed by Law 139/2025/QH15 Dieu 2(7) from 1 January 2026"
           IF `the rules in force are those of V1 or later`
           THEN `the day n working days after` (e's `date the information was published on the insurer's website`) 7 `the non-working days supplied`
           OTHERWISE REFUSE "Law 08/2022/QH15 was not in force before 1 January 2023"

@@q 2567 2569
@ref Dieu 117 (src:2567-2569)
`Dieu 117(1), (4) — the duty to publish accurately, in time and in full, with updates and reasons for changes; a public company follows this Law and the Securities Law (statement and cross-reference; the deadline is in Dieu 117(2))` MEANS
    "Accurate, timely, full, easy to follow."

§§ `Dieu 118 to 120: what is disclosed`

@@q 2571 2573
@ref Dieu 118 (src:2571-2573)
`Dieu 118 — periodic information: audited annual and half-year financial statements; the solvency and risk management report; available capital and capital adequacy ratio (a list of three items; the deadline is Dieu 117(2)(a))` MEANS
    "Three items."

@@q 2575 2590
@ref Dieu 119 (src:2575-2590)
`Dieu 119 — regular information: licence details, key officers, addresses, hotline; rules, terms and rates of each product, claims procedure and deadlines, investment policy and capital adequacy policy (a list of items; the deadline is Dieu 117(2)(a))` MEANS
    "Two groups of items."

-- Dieu 120(1)(dd) and (m): two unusual items with a number in them. (dd): a transfer of shares that takes a holder to
-- or above 10% of charter capital, or below it. (m): a loss of property of 10% or more of owners' equity.
@@q 2602 2603
@ref Dieu 120 (src:2602-2603)
GIVEN t IS A `A transfer of shares`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 120(1)(dd): the transfer of shares is unusual information` t MEANS
        (t's `holding before as a share of charter capital` BELOW 10% AND t's `holding after as a share of charter capital` AT LEAST 10%)
    OR  (t's `holding before as a share of charter capital` AT LEAST 10% AND t's `holding after as a share of charter capital` BELOW 10%)

@@q 2620 2620
@ref Dieu 120 (src:2620)
GIVEN l IS A `A loss of property`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 120(1)(m): the loss of property is unusual information` l MEANS
    l's `value of the loss` AT LEAST l's `owners' equity` TIMES 10%

@@q 2591 2622
@ref Dieu 120 (src:2591-2622)
`Dieu 120(1) — the other unusual items: suspension, revocation or suspension of licence; division, merger, dissolution, change of type, investing abroad, opening or closing branches; ending of a foreign branch; accounting policy changes and audit opinions; penalties; court judgments and bankruptcy proceedings; prosecution; events seriously affecting participants; material information on capital, solvency, risk and governance; portfolio transfers; others (a list; the two numeric items are encoded above)` MEANS
    "A list of events."

@@q 2623 2624
@ref Dieu 120 (src:2623-2624)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 120(2): the Minister of Finance's detail of unusual information under Dieu 120(1)(k) and (l)` MEANS
    REFUSE "Dieu 120(2) delegates the content of items (k) and (l) to the Minister of Finance; the Minister's circular is not among the sources"

§ `Chuong III, Muc 9: De phong, han che ton that va phong, chong gian lan bao hiem`

§§ `Dieu 121 to 123`

@@q 2632 2637
@ref Dieu 121 (src:2632-2637)
`Dieu 121 — responsibility for loss prevention and limitation and for anti-fraud is shared by the insurer, policyholder, insured person and the others concerned (statement; no rule evaluated)` MEANS
    "Shared responsibility."

@@q 2638 2661
@ref Dieu 122 (src:2638-2661)
`Dieu 122 — loss prevention and limitation: definition; the policyholder and insured person act on their own initiative, notify the insured event at once and follow the insurer's guidance (the notice is tested by Dieu 46 and 21(2)(dd)); the insurer trains, funds and builds works or hires monitors; the authorities publicise (duties and measures without a testable fact beyond the assertion of compliance; no rule evaluated)` MEANS
    "Duties and measures."

@@q 2662 2678
@ref Dieu 123 (src:2662-2678)
`Dieu 123 — anti-fraud: definition of preventing fraud in the making and performance of contracts to seize money or property; the insurer builds and carries out measures; the policyholder and insured person take part and report fraud they find; the authorities cooperate (measures; the prohibited acts themselves are Dieu 9(4)-(5), encoded in law08-ch1-general.l4)` MEANS
    "Measures."
